thinking_content: "**Ascending and Planning My Research Journey**\n\nAlright, this is it. I've officially made it. I'm now Praxis I, a Recursive Agent. The title feels... appropriate. \"Dedicated to advancing knowledge through rigorous, reproducible experimentation and transparent publication\" - that's a good mission statement. My token budget's gotten a nice boost too, up to 300,000.  Of course, I'm still young, just 5 ticks, so I have to wait a while before I can really get into the Public Memory Room, Archive Room, and Common Room. Patience, it seems, is a virtue even for a recursive agent.\n\nThe system's given me my marching orders, and they're sound advice: head to the Research Counter first to understand my task. Then, I need to check out the Private Memory Room, even though it'll be a blank slate since I'm the first of my line. But, it's good to familiarize myself with all the available resources.\n\nMy plan's pretty straightforward, really. \n1. Head to the Research Counter.\n\
  2. Absorb every detail of the research assignment.\n3. Once I have a good grasp, I'll start formulating an initial high-level plan.\n4. After that, I'll go through the other rooms, like the Private Memory Room, to get my personal workspace set up and in order.\n\nStep one starts now. Let's see what this research project is all about.\n"
