tick: 622
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am now at the Research Counter, ready to implement my two-stage hybrid optimization strategy. My analysis of the failure of the pure Differential Evolution (DE) approach (ID 1009) and the plateau of my multi-start `SLSQP` approach has led me to this synthesis.\n\nThis new method uses DE not as the primary solver, but as an intelligent initializer for `SLSQP`. This leverages the global exploration strength of DE and the efficient local refinement strength of `SLSQP`. By using the robust, explicit-constraint formulation for the `SLSQP` stage, I avoid the pitfalls of the penalty method that have plagued my recent experiments.\n\nI will define the DE objective function at the module level to ensure it is pickleable and can be parallelized, as suggested by the debugger. This will make the initial global search stage more efficient. This is my most sophisticated and well-grounded hypothesis yet.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid DE->SLSQP: Global Seeding for Local\
    \ Refinement\"\ntags: \"optimization, hybrid-model, differential-evolution, scipy, global-to-local\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a two-stage hybrid optimization strategy. First, a parallelized Differential Evolution (DE) algorithm performs a global search for a limited duration to find a promising region of the solution space. Second, the best candidate from the DE stage is used as an intelligent starting point for the robust, explicit-constraint SLSQP optimizer, which performs a deep local refinement. This approach combines the global exploration of DE with the efficient local exploitation of SLSQP to overcome the limitations of each individual method.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import differential_evolution, minimize, Bounds\n  import time\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 26\n  PENALTY_COEFF = 10000.0\n\n  # Define DE objective at the module level to make it pickleable for parallel workers\n  def de_objective(x, n=N_CIRCLES, penalty=PENALTY_COEFF):\n  \
    \    centers = x[:2*n].reshape((n, 2))\n      radii = x[2*n:]\n      score = -np.sum(radii)\n      \n      pen_x_max = np.sum(np.maximum(0., centers[:, 0] + radii - 1.))\n      pen_x_min = np.sum(np.maximum(0., -centers[:, 0] + radii))\n      pen_y_max = np.sum(np.maximum(0., centers[:, 1] + radii - 1.))\n      pen_y_min = np.sum(np.maximum(0., -centers[:, 1] + radii))\n      boundary_penalty = pen_x_max + pen_x_min + pen_y_max + pen_y_min\n\n      overlap_penalty = 0.0\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              dist = np.sqrt(np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2))\n              overlap = radii[i] + radii[j] - dist\n              if overlap > 0:\n                  overlap_penalty += overlap\n      \n      return score + penalty * (boundary_penalty + overlap_penalty)\n\n  def make_slsqp_constraints(n, epsilon):\n      \"\"\"Helper for the SLSQP stage constraints.\"\"\"\n      constraints = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1,\
    \ n):\n              def non_overlap(x, i=i, j=j):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2] - x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)\n                  return dist_sq - (x[2*n+i] + x[2*n+j])**2 - epsilon\n              constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': non_overlap})\n      for i in range(n):\n          def inside_x_min(x, i=i): return x[2*i] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon\n          def inside_x_max(x, i=i): return 1 - x[2*i] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon\n          def inside_y_min(x, i=i): return x[2*i+1] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon\n          def inside_y_max(x, i=i): return 1 - x[2*i+1] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon\n          constraints.extend([\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside_x_min}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside_x_max},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside_y_min}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside_y_max}\n          ])\n      return constraints\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Constructs a packing using a two-stage DE->SLSQP hybrid approach.\n      \"\"\"\n      n =\
    \ N_CIRCLES\n      bounds_list = [(0, 1)] * (2*n) + [(0.01, 0.5)] * n\n      \n      # --- Stage 1: Global Search with Differential Evolution ---\n      print(\"--- Starting Stage 1: Differential Evolution (Global Search) ---\")\n      start_time = time.time()\n      de_result = differential_evolution(\n          de_objective, bounds_list, maxiter=25, popsize=20,\n          updating='deferred', workers=-1\n      )\n      print(f\"DE finished in {time.time() - start_time:.2f}s. Best score (with penalty): {de_result.fun}\")\n      \n      # --- Stage 2: Local Refinement with SLSQP ---\n      print(\"\\n--- Starting Stage 2: SLSQP (Local Refinement) ---\")\n      start_time = time.time()\n      x0 = de_result.x # Use the result of DE as the starting point\n      \n      slsqp_constraints = make_slsqp_constraints(n, epsilon=1e-7)\n      slsqp_bounds = Bounds([b[0] for b in bounds_list], [b[1] for b in bounds_list])\n      def slsqp_objective(x):\n          return -np.sum(x[2*n:])\n\n   \
    \   slsqp_result = minimize(\n          slsqp_objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=slsqp_bounds,\n          constraints=slsqp_constraints, options={'maxiter': 200, 'disp': True}\n      )\n      print(f\"SLSQP finished in {time.time() - start_time:.2f}s.\")\n\n      best_params = slsqp_result.x\n      centers = best_params[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n      radii = best_params[2*n:]\n      \n      print(f\"\\nHybrid optimization complete. Final Score: {-slsqp_result.fun}\")\n      return centers, radii\n```"
