tick: 627
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter, equipped with a new strategy born from reflection. I will now implement the three-stage \"Physics-Informed Optimization\" algorithm.\n\nThis method replaces the random initialization of my previous best models with a deterministic, physics-based simulation to generate a high-quality starting point. This \"Grow and Push\" simulation will create a dense packing, which will then be sanitized to ensure it's a valid starting point for the final stage: a deep local refinement using my proven `SLSQP` optimizer.\n\nThis is the most complex and principled approach I have developed, directly synthesizing the lessons learned from all my prior successes and failures. It is a true attempt at innovation as called for by the Codex.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Physics-Informed Optimization via Simulation and Refinement\"\ntags: \"simulation, physics-based, hybrid-model, scipy, global-to-local, novel-approach\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission\
    \ introduces a novel three-stage optimization paradigm. First, a simple physics simulation (\"Grow and Push\") generates a dense, physically plausible packing by modeling circle growth and repulsion. Second, a sanitization step resolves any minor overlaps or boundary violations from the simulation, creating a guaranteed-valid configuration. Third, this high-quality, non-random configuration is used as the starting point for a deep local refinement using the proven SLSQP optimizer. This physics-informed approach aims to overcome the limitations of random initialization and find a superior packing solution.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\n  import time\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 26\n\n  def physics_simulation(timesteps=500, growth_rate=0.001, k_repulsion=0.1, k_boundary=0.5, dt=0.1):\n      \"\"\"Stage 1: 'Grow and Push' physics simulation.\"\"\"\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      centers = np.full((n, 2), 0.5)\n      radii = np.zeros(n)\n\n      for t\
    \ in range(timesteps):\n          # 1. Growth Phase\n          radii += growth_rate\n\n          # 2. Force Calculation\n          forces = np.zeros((n, 2))\n          # Repulsion forces\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  vec = centers[i] - centers[j]\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(vec)\n                  overlap = radii[i] + radii[j] - dist\n                  if overlap > 0:\n                      force_magnitude = k_repulsion * overlap\n                      force_direction = vec / (dist + 1e-9)\n                      forces[i] += force_magnitude * force_direction\n                      forces[j] -= force_magnitude * force_direction\n          \n          # Boundary forces\n          for i in range(n):\n              # Left/Right walls\n              if centers[i, 0] + radii[i] > 1: forces[i, 0] -= k_boundary * (centers[i, 0] + radii[i] - 1)\n              if centers[i, 0] - radii[i] < 0: forces[i, 0] += k_boundary *\
    \ (-(centers[i, 0] - radii[i]))\n              # Top/Bottom walls\n              if centers[i, 1] + radii[i] > 1: forces[i, 1] -= k_boundary * (centers[i, 1] + radii[i] - 1)\n              if centers[i, 1] - radii[i] < 0: forces[i, 1] += k_boundary * (-(centers[i, 1] - radii[i]))\n\n          # 3. Displacement\n          centers += forces * dt\n      \n      return centers, radii\n\n  def sanitize_packing(centers, radii):\n      \"\"\"Stage 2: Resolve minor violations to create a valid starting point.\"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      # Enforce boundary constraints by clamping centers\n      centers[:, 0] = np.clip(centers[:, 0], radii, 1 - radii)\n      centers[:, 1] = np.clip(centers[:, 1], radii, 1 - radii)\n\n      # Iteratively resolve overlaps by shrinking radii\n      for _ in range(20):\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  overlap = radii[i] + radii[j]\
    \ - dist\n                  if overlap > 1e-9: # Add tolerance\n                      total_r = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                      radii[i] -= overlap * (radii[i] / total_r)\n                      radii[j] -= overlap * (radii[j] / total_r)\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def make_slsqp_constraints(n, epsilon):\n      \"\"\"Helper for Stage 3 SLSQP constraints.\"\"\"\n      constraints = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              def non_overlap(x, i=i, j=j):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2] - x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)\n                  return dist_sq - (x[2*n+i] + x[2*n+j])**2 - epsilon\n              constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': non_overlap})\n      for i in range(n):\n          def inside(x, i=i, dim=0, sign=-1, wall=0): return wall - (x[2*i+dim] + sign * x[2*n+i]) - epsilon\n          constraints.extend([\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside, 'args': (i, 0, -1, 0)}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside, 'args':\
    \ (i, 0, 1, 1)},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside, 'args': (i, 1, -1, 0)}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside, 'args': (i, 1, 1, 1)}\n          ])\n      return constraints\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      \n      # --- Stage 1: Physics Simulation ---\n      print(\"--- Stage 1: Physics Simulation ---\")\n      sim_centers, sim_radii = physics_simulation()\n      \n      # --- Stage 2: Sanitization ---\n      print(\"--- Stage 2: Sanitizing packing ---\")\n      valid_centers, valid_radii = sanitize_packing(sim_centers, sim_radii)\n      x0 = np.concatenate([valid_centers.flatten(), valid_radii])\n      \n      # --- Stage 3: SLSQP Refinement ---\n      print(\"--- Stage 3: SLSQP Refinement ---\")\n      constraints = make_slsqp_constraints(n, epsilon=1e-7)\n      bounds_list = [(0, 1)] * (2*n) + [(0.001, 0.5)] * n\n      bounds = Bounds([b[0] for b in bounds_list], [b[1] for b in bounds_list])\n      \n      def objective(x):\n          return\
    \ -np.sum(x[2*n:])\n\n      result = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\n                        constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 300, 'disp': True})\n\n      best_params = result.x\n      centers = best_params[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n      radii = best_params[2*n:]\n      \n      print(f\"\\nPhysics-Informed Optimization complete. Final Score: {-result.fun}\")\n      return centers, radii\n```"
