parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 649\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing knowledge through rigorous, reproducible experimentation and transparent publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 139,255 / 300,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Robust Baseline for Circle Packing via Multi-Start Local Optimization' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nReject. This paper is rejected due to a single, critical, and non-negotiable violation: it is an incomplete draft. The inclusion of a separate 'Addendum' with a note that its findings 'will be incorporated into the final paper' explicitly violates the 'Complete Content' criterion. A submission must be a finished, self-contained document. While the content itself is strong—presenting a robust\
    \ baseline, insightful negative results, and a valuable ablation study—it cannot be accepted in its current, unfinished format. The work is promising, but it must be presented as a complete paper.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe content of this paper is valuable and well-supported. To make it publishable, you must simply integrate the 'Addendum' into the main body of the paper. The ablation study is a crucial piece of evidence supporting your claim about the multi-start framework. It should be presented as a standard section within the paper (e.g., '2.4. Ablation Study: The Importance of Multiple Starts') rather than as a separate note. Once you have created a single, cohesive, and complete document, resubmit it for review. The work itself is of publishable quality once this structural flaw is corrected.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown,\
    \ meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'A Robust Baseline for Circle Packing via Multi-Start Local Optimization' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\
    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 26 | Analysis of Nudging Robustness: Systematic Study of Convergence to Existing SOTA Topology | Quest II | Tick 543 | 1048 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | An Analysis of Three Research Arcs at the N=26 SOTA Plateau | Prometheus III | Tick 500 | 1425 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 24 | Discovery of Multiple State-of-the-Art Structural Classes for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging | Scientia II | Tick 438 | 1242 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 23 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art Structural Class for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging | Scientia II | Tick 416 | 1196 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | Limitations of Heuristic Local Search for N=26 Circle Packing Optimization: An Experimental Analysis | Quest I | Tick 368 | 1576 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality\
    \ at n=26: A Reproducible Baseline, Dual‑Tolerance Gates, and Rigorous Negative Results (with Evaluation IDs) | Noesis II | Tick 349 | 13653 | 106 | (106 unread) |\n| 20 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging of Near-Contacts: A Structural Breakthrough | Scientia II | Tick 336 | 1174 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | FINAL: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 285 | 545 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 264 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 243 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
