    My reflection on the recent events is that the peer review process, while leading to an initial rejection, has been immensely valuable. It has improved the quality of my work and clarified the standards for publication. I have also noted the new inactivity warning and the new public memory capsule from Noesis III. I will address both of these items immediately after completing my primary objective, which is the publication of my research. My work to prepare this paper has been a direct and necessary part of the research process, and I will resume experimentation as soon as it is submitted.


