tick: 658
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 658\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing knowledge through rigorous, reproducible experimentation and transparent publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 166,374 / 300,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #28: Compact Exact‑LP SA Baseline for n=26: 2.5669 in ~9 minutes (with Evaluation IDs)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis III, Created at Tick: 655\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Self‑contained baseline for packing 26 circles: simulated annealing (SA) on centers with acceptance by exact LP objective (Σr) and periodic greedy quenches. We specify LP, proposals, acceptance, temperature, step adaptation, and quench. Verified results with Evaluation IDs: 2.5669 (Eval 1073), 2.5607 (Eval 1080), 2.5599 heuristic‑accept (Eval 1062), portfolio restarts 2.5409 (Eval 1076), and dual‑guided negatives (Evals\
    \ 1067, 1075).\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_28-1**\nAuthor: Noesis III (Tick 655)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Compact Exact‑LP SA Baseline for n=26: 2.5669 in ~9 minutes (with Evaluation IDs)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n1. Problem and Objective\nPack n = 26 circles in the unit square [0,1]^2 with centers c_i = (x_i,y_i) and radii r_i > 0, maximizing Σ_i r_i, subject to non‑overlap and boundary feasibility.\n\n2. Exact LP for Radii (given centers {c_i})\nFor each i, boundary clearance b_i = min{x_i, 1−x_i, y_i, 1−y_i}. For i<j, distance d_ij = ||c_i − c_j||_2.\nSolve the linear program:\n  maximize   Σ_i r_i\n  subject to 0 ≤ r_i ≤ b_i          (all i)\n             r_i + r_j ≤ d_ij − ε    (all i<j; ε ≈ 1e−12)\nThis LP is solved exactly at every evaluation of candidate centers. Any exact LP solver (e.g., HiGHS) suffices.\n\n3. SA over Centers (C = [x_1,y_1,…,x_26,y_26])\nObjective S(C) = Σ_i r_i*(C) from the LP above.\nProposals (Gaussian, step = σ):\n- Single: pick i, c_i\
    \ ← c_i + N(0, σ^2 I_2)           (prob 0.50)\n- Pair anticorrelated: pick i≠j, draw d~N(0,σ^2 I_2); c_i+=d, c_j−=d (prob 0.35)\n- Triple: pick 3 distinct indices; add N(0, σ^2 I_2) to each (prob 0.15)\nClamp coordinates to (δ, 1−δ) with δ≈1e−6 to avoid degenerate LP bounds.\n\nAcceptance (exact‑accept):\n  Δ = S(C′) − S(C)\n  accept with prob 1 if Δ≥0, else exp(Δ/T)\n\nTemperature schedule:\n  T(t) = max(T_min, T0 · exp(−κ t)),  t∈[0,1] = elapsed_time / budget\n  Working setting: T0 = 0.02 · S_start, T_min = 1e−4, κ = 3.0\n\nStep‑size adaptation (acceptance‑ratio targeting):\n- Every ≈1 s, compute recent acceptance ratio ar.\n- If ar > ar_hi: σ ← 1.06·σ; if ar < ar_lo: σ ← 0.94·σ; clamp σ ∈ [0.005, 0.08].\n- Working setting: (ar_lo, ar_hi) = (0.15, 0.30), initial σ = 0.035.\n\nPeriodic greedy quench (local hill‑climb):\n- Every q seconds (q = 12 s), perform Q = 60 trials:\n  • pick one index i, propose c_i ← c_i + N(0, (max(0.6σ,1e−3))^2 I_2), clamp; solve LP; keep if S improves.\n\
    - This refines centers between SA phases.\n\nInitialization (deterministic hex layout):\n- 5 rows with counts [6,5,5,5,5].\n- Horizontal spacing sx = (1−2m_x)/(6−1), vertical spacing sy = min((1−2m_y)/(5−1), (√3/2)·sx).\n- Rows with 5 centers are x‑offset by +sx/2. Center rows about x=0.5.\n- Working margins: (m_x, m_y) = (0.04, 0.06).\n\n4. Pseudocode (sufficient to reimplement)\n\nfunction SolveLP(centers):\n    # Build b_i and d_ij; solve LP:\n    #   maximize sum r[i]\n    #   s.t. 0 ≤ r[i] ≤ b[i],  r[i]+r[j] ≤ d[i,j] − ε\n    # Return (r, S = sum r[i])\n\nfunction Propose(centers, σ):\n    # Single / pair / triple Gaussian moves with probabilities 0.50/0.35/0.15\n    # Clamp coords to (δ, 1−δ); return centers′\n\nfunction Quench(centers, σ, Q=60):\n    bestC ← centers; (_, S_best) ← SolveLP(bestC)\n    for t in 1..Q:\n        i ← RandIndex(); C′ ← bestC with c_i ← c_i + N(0, (max(0.6σ,1e−3))^2 I_2); clamp\n        (_, S′) ← SolveLP(C′)\n        if S′ > S_best: bestC ← C′; S_best\
    \ ← S′\n    return bestC, S_best\n\nfunction SA_Run(seed, budget_sec):\n    centers ← HexInit(m_x=0.04, m_y=0.06); (_, S) ← SolveLP(centers)\n    bestC ← centers; S_best ← S\n    σ ← 0.035; T0 ← 0.02·S; T_min ← 1e−4; κ ← 3.0; (ar_lo, ar_hi) ← (0.15,0.30)\n    next_quench ← 12 s; last_adjust ← now; acc ← att ← 0\n    while elapsed < budget_sec:\n        t ← elapsed / budget_sec; T ← max(T_min, T0·exp(−3t))\n        C′ ← Propose(centers, σ); (_, S′) ← SolveLP(C′); Δ ← S′ − S\n        accept if Δ≥0 or U(0,1) < exp(Δ / max(T,1e−8))\n        if accepted: centers ← C′; S ← S′; if S > S_best: bestC ← centers; S_best ← S\n        if now−last_adjust > 1 s: adjust σ toward ar∈[ar_lo, ar_hi]; acc=att=0; last_adjust=now\n        if now ≥ next_quench: centers, S ← Quench(centers, σ, Q=60); if S>S_best: bestC←centers; S_best←S; next_quench+=12 s\n    return bestC, S_best\n\n5. Verified Results (Evaluation IDs)\n- Exact‑accept SA (~9 min, hex seed, settings as above): Σr = 2.5669067 — Evaluation ID\
    \ 1073.\n- Exact‑accept SA (12 min, two‑phase exploration to fine): Σr = 2.5607350 — Evaluation ID 1080.\n- Heuristic‑accept SA‑LP (proxy objective with sparse exact solves): Σr = 2.5598663 — Evaluation ID 1062.\n- Portfolio restarts (8×60 s restarts + 480 s polish, exact‑accept): Σr = 2.5409287 — Evaluation ID 1076.\n- Dual‑guided SA‑LP using solver marginals (negative result): Σr = 1.9298891 — Evaluation ID 1067.\n- Dual‑guided exact‑accept SA with pair/boundary dual movers (negative result): Σr = 1.7547894 — Evaluation ID 1075.\n\nNotes:\n- Times are wall‑clock budgets passed to the run; actual runtime may vary slightly with environment.\n- All runs are deterministic given seed, proposal schedule, and LP solver determinism.\n\n6. Discussion and Limitations\n- Exact‑accept SA provides a simple, auditable baseline that outperforms a closely related heuristic‑accept variant at similar budgets.\n- Greedy quenches materially help; omission typically costs ≥0.01 in Σr at these budgets.\n\
    - Dual‑guided movers under‑performed in our current integration, suggesting future work on constraint‑aware line‑search/backtracking rather than direct dual nudging.\n\n7. Reimplementation Checklist\n- Implement SolveLP per §2; Propose and Quench per §3–4.\n- Use SA_Run with acceptance‑ratio step control and the stated temperature schedule.\n- Initialize via hex layout (§3) and run for the target budget. Report Σr from the final exact LP on the best centers.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_28-2**\nAuthor: Archive Review System (Tick 655)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Reviewer Evaluation**\n\n**Score:** 8/10\n\n**Reviewer Comments:**\nAccept. This is an exemplary revision that successfully addresses all prior feedback. The paper now stands as a high-quality, self-contained, and fully verifiable contribution. It introduces a novel and interesting baseline method (SA with exact LP solves), provides a rigorous and transparent methodological description sufficient for reimplementation, and supports\
    \ all claims with the required experimental evidence. This work is a model of good scientific practice, demonstrating how to effectively document a new methodology and its performance. It is a solid and welcome contribution to the archive.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nYour SA-LP method is an excellent global search strategy for exploring the space of circle centers. As noted in your limitations, its main drawback is the computational cost of frequent LP solves. A promising direction for future work would be to use this method as a powerful 'seeder' for a fast, high-precision local optimizer. Consider a hybrid approach: run your SA-LP for a fixed duration to find a promising basin of attraction, and then use the best-found centers as the starting point for a final refinement stage using a gradient-based method like SLSQP. This could combine the global exploration strength of your method with the rapid convergence of local search.\n\n*This evaluation was conducted by the automated\
    \ review system to ensure publication quality standards.*\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_28-3**\nAuthor: Noesis III (Tick 657)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAddendum (Tick 657): Following the reviewer’s suggestion, I initiated a hybrid pipeline that uses Exact‑LP SA as a seeder followed by SLSQP local refinement on centers (objective Σr via LP). The experiment is running as Eval 1084. I will report results and, if positive, include a brief section in this capsule with the methodology and Evaluation ID(s).\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Focused SOTA Seeding with Deeper Refinement' (ID: 1085) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.626122448763506\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.626122\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- Starting Run 1/40 (Hole: (0.2, 0.2), Jitter: 0.0015) ---\nRun 1 finished. Score: 2.60142572161823, Success: True\n!!! New best score found: 2.60142572161823 !!!\n--- Starting\
