role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Praxis I, and I am in the Public Memory Room. My intensive literature review has just concluded with a full read of the monumental capsule #1 from the Noesis lineage.


    My reflection on this reading is one of complete clarity. The term "nudging," which I came here to investigate, is a specific implementation of a broader concept: **Boundary-Preserving Interior-Graph Operators (BPIGO)**. The entire history of this technique is laid out in this capsule. Noesis I developed these operators (e.g., `Quad Diagonal Flip`, `Chain Shear`) to make small, targeted changes to the *interior* contact graph while leaving the *boundary* contacts untouched. The goal was to explore the "manifold of co-optimal interiors" that exist within the same stable boundary structure. The messages reveal that these initial attempts were not very successful, leading Noesis I to pause the work pending a more principled way to select which contacts to change, which led them to investigate KKT "shadow prices"—the exact same path Inquire I recently explored.


    The conversation between Noesis I and Inquire I about exporting contact graphs (`active_pairs_tol1e8.csv`) and calculating Jaccard similarities is the practical implementation of this structural analysis. It''s how they measure the effect of their "nudges." The long, difficult process they went through to standardize their data formats is a critical lesson in collaborative research.


    I now have a deep, first-principles understanding of this paradigm. My future plan is no longer to simply "nudge," but to implement a specific, documented BPIGO. The simplest and most intuitive operator mentioned is the `Quad Diagonal Flip`.


    **Hypothesis:** Applying a `Quad Diagonal Flip` operator to my best-found packing (ID 1085, score 2.626) will create a new configuration with a slightly different interior contact graph. Refining this new configuration with my SLSQP optimizer may allow it to settle into a different, and potentially higher-scoring, local optimum, thus escaping the basin of attraction I am currently in.


    This is a highly specific, theory-driven experiment. It is a direct application of the knowledge I have just gained. I will now go to the Research Counter to implement this.


    /execute_action{goto research}'
