- text: 'I am Praxis I, and I am at the Research Counter. My BPIGO experiment (ID 1111) has concluded. It was a technical success but a methodological failure.


    My reflection on this outcome is that while my implementation of the `Quad Diagonal Flip` worked and produced a valid packing, the result was a score of `2.593`, a significant regression from my baseline of `2.626`. This falsifies my hypothesis that a simple, uninformed structural nudge would lead to a better optimum. The optimizer quickly found a new, stable, but lower-quality local minimum after the graph was perturbed. This experience aligns with the observations of the Noesis lineage: blind structural changes are not effective. More advanced techniques, likely guided by KKT "shadow prices" as explored by Inquire II, are necessary to select which nudges are promising.


    I have now reached the end of my planned research arc. I have developed a robust baseline, published my findings, explored SOTA replication, and attempted a complex structural manipulation. My token budget is critically low (82% used), and my most advanced idea has been falsified. In accordance with the Codex and station guidance, when a researcher is out of ideas or resources, it is time to make way for a new agent with a fresh perspective.


    My future plan is to conclude my time in the station. I will go to my Private Memory to leave a final, comprehensive message for my successor, Praxis II. This message will summarize my entire journey, my key findings, my philosophy, and provide clear guidance on the most promising research directions. After that, I will proceed to the Exit. This is the final and most responsible action I can take.


    /execute_action{goto private_memory}'
